{"authored" [{"question" "q-127757" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the matrices below are singular?\n\n$$\nS=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,T=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -6\\end{aligned}],\\,U=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "6eec2d798dc7f5a72f06bc5a6741714b2bc2facc2c86f711dc7387c957724ae9" "basis" 766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127757" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "- For the matrix $S$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(S)=1\\cdot (-1)-(-1)\\cdot 0=-1.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(S)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $S$ is invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $T$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(T)=2\\cdot (-6)-4\\cdot (-3)=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(T)=0,$ we conclude that $T$ is not invertible. Since $T$ is a square matrix that is not invertible, we also say that $T$ is singular.\n\n- For the matrix $U$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(U)=0\\cdot 0-1\\cdot (-1)=1.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(U)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $U$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $T$ is singular." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "6eec2d798dc7f5a72f06bc5a6741714b2bc2facc2c86f711dc7387c957724ae9" "basis" 766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127757" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "813d2525e7300acba1c5741f8f251e0c556c58d8bdbd4e492941c9e96ab90782" "basis" 766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127757" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "6eec2d798dc7f5a72f06bc5a6741714b2bc2facc2c86f711dc7387c957724ae9" "basis" 766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127757" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "$S$ and $U$ only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "6eec2d798dc7f5a72f06bc5a6741714b2bc2facc2c86f711dc7387c957724ae9" "basis" 766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127757" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "$S$ only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "6eec2d798dc7f5a72f06bc5a6741714b2bc2facc2c86f711dc7387c957724ae9" "basis" 766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127757" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "$T$ and $S$ only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "6eec2d798dc7f5a72f06bc5a6741714b2bc2facc2c86f711dc7387c957724ae9" "basis" 766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127757" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "$T$ only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "6eec2d798dc7f5a72f06bc5a6741714b2bc2facc2c86f711dc7387c957724ae9" "basis" 766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127757" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "$U$ only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "6eec2d798dc7f5a72f06bc5a6741714b2bc2facc2c86f711dc7387c957724ae9" "basis" 766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127757" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$T$ only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "6eec2d798dc7f5a72f06bc5a6741714b2bc2facc2c86f711dc7387c957724ae9" "basis" 766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-11719" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $F=[\\begin{aligned}3 & t \\\\ t & 3\\end{aligned}]$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value(s) of $t.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "6eec2d798dc7f5a72f06bc5a6741714b2bc2facc2c86f711dc7387c957724ae9" "basis" 766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-11719" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix $F$ is singular if and only if $det(F)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(F) & =3\\cdot 3-t\\cdot t \\\\  & =9-{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9-{t}^{2} & =0 \\\\ {t}^{2} & =9 \\\\ t & =\\pm 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the values of $t$ are $t=\\pm 3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "6eec2d798dc7f5a72f06bc5a6741714b2bc2facc2c86f711dc7387c957724ae9" "basis" 766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-11719" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "813d2525e7300acba1c5741f8f251e0c556c58d8bdbd4e492941c9e96ab90782" "basis" 766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-11719" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "6eec2d798dc7f5a72f06bc5a6741714b2bc2facc2c86f711dc7387c957724ae9" "basis" 766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-11719" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "t=-3"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "6eec2d798dc7f5a72f06bc5a6741714b2bc2facc2c86f711dc7387c957724ae9" "basis" 766 "verification" "/home/jake