 "value" "Which of the matrices below does **not** have an inverse?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 15 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979417/state.json" "file_sha256" "5c883a2e5de1eeebb6a3e52c4ea740ce8fa1bb3890e192b9895aff80945bcf13" "basis" 851 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979417/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127826" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "- The matrix $A$ is a $3\\times 1$ matrix. So, it is not invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $B$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(B)=-3\\cdot 5-1\\cdot 15=-30.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(B)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $B$ is invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $C$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(C)=7\\cdot 2-3\\cdot 4=2.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(C)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $C$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $A$ does not have an inverse." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979417/state.json" "file_sha256" "5c883a2e5de1eeebb6a3e52c4ea740ce8fa1bb3890e192b9895aff80945bcf13" "basis" 851 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979417/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127826" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979417/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5e145fb97abb632207d6c68caf0fb1c3e75e785931de38c4da626620ab90b1a2" "basis" 851 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979417/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127826" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio 