ture-workers/linear/14076113/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "dfff988c22e0696093af3464517e00331d588c2ca367315b8f8dfc0665dc3c7b"} {"question" "q-11719" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076113/state.json" "file_sha256" "66160ceb7d5d6edb478939b97c756f24379b41f4d19c8d60d47f8f28557e778b"} {"question" "q-11719" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "t=-3"] ["math" "t=2"] ["math" "t=3"] ["math" "t=\\pm 2"] ["math" "t=\\pm 3"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076113/state.json" "file_sha256" "66160ceb7d5d6edb478939b97c756f24379b41f4d19c8d60d47f8f28557e778b"} {"question" "q-11719" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "t=\\pm 3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076113/state.json" "file_sha256" "66160ceb7d5d6edb478939b97c756f24379b41f4d19c8d60d47f8f28557e778b"} {"question" "q-71935" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the matrices below are singular?\n\n$$\nN=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,V=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,Z=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 8 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076113/state.json" "file_sha256" "66160ceb7d5d6edb478939b97c756f24379b41f4d19c8d60d47f8f28557e778b"} {"question" "q-71935" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "- For the matrix $N$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(N)=3\\cdot 0-0\\cdot 1=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(N)=0,$ we conclude that $N$ is not invertible. Since $N$ is a square matrix that is not invertible, we also say that $N$ is singular.\n\n- The matrix $V$ is a $5\\times 1$ matrix. So, it is not invertible. Since the matrix is not square, we can't say that it's singular.\n\n- For the matrix $Z$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(Z)=0\\cdot 0-2\\cdot 8=-16.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(Z)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $Z$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $N$ is singular." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076113/state.json" "file_sha256" "66160ceb7d5d6edb478939b97c756f24379b41f4d19c8d60d47f8f28557e778b"} {"question" "q-71935" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076113/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "dfff988c22e0696093af3464517e00331d588c2ca367315b8f8dfc0665dc3c7b"} {"question" "q-71935" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076113/state.json" "file_sha256" "66160ceb7d5d6edb478939b97c756f24379b41f4d19c8d60d47f8f28557e778b"} {"question" "q-71935" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$N$ and $V$ only"] ["text" "$N$ and $Z$ only"] ["text" "$N$ only"] ["text" "$V$ and $Z$ only"] ["text" "$Z$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076113/state.json" "file_sha256" "66160ceb7d5d6edb478939b97c756f24379b41f4d19c8d60d47f8f28557e778b"} {"question" "q-71935" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$N$ only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076113/state.json" "file_sha256" "66160ceb7d5d6edb478939b97c756f24379b41f4d19c8d60d47f8f28557e778b"} {"question" "q-127757" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the matrices below are singular?\n\n$$\nS=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,T=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -6\\end{aligned}],\\,U=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076113/state.json" "file_sha256" "66160ceb7d5d6edb478939b97c756f24379b41f4d19c8d60d47f8f28557e778b"} {"question" "q-127757" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "- For the matrix $S$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(S)=1\\cdot (-1)-(-1)\\cdot 0=-1.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(S)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $S$ is invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $T$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(T)=2\\cdot (-6)-4\\cdot (-3)=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(T)=0,$ we conclude that $T$ is not invertible. Since $T$ is a square matrix that is not invertible, we also say that $T$ is singular.\n\n- For the matrix $U$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(U)=0\\cdot 0-1\\cdot (-1)=1.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(U)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $U$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $T$ is singular." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076113/state.json" "file_sha256" "66160ceb7d5d6edb478939b97c756f24379b41f4d19c8d60d47f8f28557e778b"} {"question" "q-127757" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076113/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "dfff988c22e0696093af3464517e00331d588c2ca367315b8f8dfc0665dc3c7b"} {"question" "q-127757" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076113/state.json" "file_sha256" "66160ceb7d5d6edb478939b97c756f24379b41f4d19c8d60d47f8f28557e778b"} {"question" "q-127757" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$S$ and $U$ only"] ["text" "$S$ only"] ["text" "$T$ and $S$ only"] ["text" "$T$ only"] ["text" "$U$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076113/state.json" "file_sha256" "66160ceb7d5d6edb478939b97c756f24379b41f4d19c8d60d47f8f28557e778b"} {"question" "q-127757" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$T$ only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076113/state.json" "file_sha256" "66160ceb7d5d6edb478939b97c756f24379b41f4d19c8d60d47f8f28557e778b"} {"question" "q-127826" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the matrices below does **not** have an inverse?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 15 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076113/state.json" "file_sha256" "66160ceb7d5d6edb478939b97c756f24379b41f4d19c8d60d47f8f28557e778b"} {"question" "q-127826" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "- The matrix $A$ is a $3\\times 1$ matrix. So, it is not invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $B$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(B)=-3\\cdot 5-1\\cdot 15=-30.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(B)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $B$ is invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $C$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(C)=7\\cdot 2-3\\cdot 4=2.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(C)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $C$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $A$ does not have an inverse." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076113/state.json" "file_sha256" "66160ceb7d5d6edb478939b97c756f24379b41f4d19c8d60d47f8f28557e778b"} {"question" "q-127826" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076113/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "dfff988c22e0696093af3464517e00331d588c2ca367315b8f8dfc0665dc3c7b"} {"question" "q-127826" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076113/state.json" "file_sha256" "66160ceb7d5d6edb478939b97c756f24379b41f4d19c8d60d47f8f28557e778b"} {"question" "q-127826" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$A$ and $B$ only"] ["text" "$A$ and $C$ only"] ["text" "$A$ only"] ["text" "$B$ and $C$ only"] ["text" "$B$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076113/state.json" "file_sha256" "66160ceb7d5d6edb478939b97c756f24379b41f4d19c8d60d47f8f28557e778b"} {"question" "q-127826" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$A$ only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076113/state.json" "file_sha256" "66160ceb7d5d6edb478939b97c756f24379b41f4d19c8d60d47f8f28557e778b"} {"question" "q-316829" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $B=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -x+7 \\\\ x-5 & 0\\end{aligned}]$\nbe a singular matrix. **In ascending order**, the values of $x$ are\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076113/state.json" "file_sha256" "66160ceb7d5d6edb478939b97c756f24379b41f4d19c8d60d47f8f28557e778b"} {"question" "q-316829" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix $B$ is singular if and only if $det(B)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =3\\cdot 0-(-x+7)\\cdot (x-5) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-5x-7x+35 \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-12x+35.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-12x+35 & =0 \\\\ (x-7)(x-5) & =0 \\\\ x & =7,5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the values of $x$ are\n\n$$\nx=5\\,\\text{and}\\,x=7.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076113/state.json" "file_sha256" "66160ceb7d5d6edb478939b97c756f24379b41f4d19c8d60d47f8f28557e778b"} {"question" "q-316829" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076113/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "dfff988c22e0696093af3464517e00331d588c2ca367315b8f8dfc0665dc3c7b"} {"question" "q-316829" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076113/state.json" "file_sha256" "66160ceb7d5d6edb478939b97c756f24379b41f4d19c8d60d47f8f28557e778b"} {"question" "q-316829" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076113/state.json" "file_sha256" "66160ceb7d5d6edb478939b97c756f24379b41f4d19c8d60d47f8f28557e778b"} {"question" "q-316829" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "m